    "title": "Local man dedicates retirement time to Honor Flight trips to D.C. for veterans - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Reports ,\n1 days ago WAYNESBORO, Pa. — Eric Haskins is dedicating his retirement years to making sure local veterans get the thank-you they’ve earned. Haskins lives at Presbyterian Senior Living’s Quincy Village in Waynesboro. He and his wife moved there two years ago from Northern Virginia, where Eric was an active volunteer for the local Honor Flight chapter. He had traveled with the nonprofit organization on 43 “missions,” escorting groups of veterans on bus trips to Washington, D.C., to visit the war memorials built in their honor and helping to celebrate them for their service and sacrifice. Read full article",
